[11.265178, "o", "  │ \u001b[97mThe theory of relativity, comprising special relativity and \u001b[0m\r\n  │ \u001b[97mgeneral relativity, fundamentally changed our understanding of \u001b[0m\r\n  │ \u001b[97mspace, time, and gravity. Special relativity, introduced by \u001b[0m\r\n  │ \u001b[97mAlbert Einstein in 1905, posits that the laws of physics are the \u001b[0m\r\n  │ \u001b[97msame for all non-accelerating observers, and that the speed of \u001b[0m\r\n  │ \u001b[97mlight within a vacuum is the same no matter the speed at which \u001b[0m\r\n  │ \u001b[97man observer travels. General relativity, published in 1915, \u001b[0m\r\n  │ \u001b[97mextends the theory to include acceleration and introduces the \u001b[0m\r\n  │ \u001b[97mconc\u001b[0m\r\n  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
